 jar lands on the test classpath — there's no wiring, config class, or bootstrap step a test project needs to perform, which is a big part of why no extra setup is needed here.\n\nThe jar also ships `META-INF/spring/...AutoConfigureMetrics.imports`, listing the auto-configuration classes (`MetricsAutoConfiguration`, `SimpleMetricsExportAutoConfiguration`, etc.) that the `@AutoConfigureMetrics` annotation pulls in. All of those classes live in `spring-boot-micrometer-metrics`/`spring-boot-micrometer-observation`, which are already *compile*-scope transitive dependencies of this artifact's own POM — so Gradle resolves them for free without any `deterministic_setup` dependency entry.\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`\n\nBased on direct inspection of the resolved POM and jar contents (not just the issue text), here's the decision:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"action\": \"no_action\",\n  \"summary\": \"Pure test-support SPI module (one annotation + one ContextCustomizerFactory, registered via bundled META-INF/spring.factories). All classes it activates (MetricsAutoConfiguration, SimpleMetricsExportAutoConfiguration, CompositeMeterRegistryAutoConfiguration, ObservationAutoConfiguration) are already transitive compile dependencies via spring-boot-micrometer-metrics and spring-boot-micrometer-observation, declared on this artifact's own POM alongside spring-boot-test-autoconfigure and micrometer-observation-test. No Docker, external service, or environment/system property is required — it's an in-process Spring test-context customizer with zero network or native-OS surface.\",\n  \"deterministic_setup\": [],\n  \"agent_guidance\": \"This artifact only ships org.springframework.boot.micrometer.metrics.test.autoconfigure.AutoConfigureMetrics and MetricsContextCustomizerFactory (+ nested DisableMetricsExportContextCustomizer). Without @AutoConfigureMetrics on a @SpringBootTest class, the customizer forces metrics export off for that test context; with it present, CompositeMeterRegistryAutoConfiguration/MetricsAutoConfiguration/SimpleMetricsExportAutoConfiguration/ObservationAutoConfiguration are auto-imported so a MeterRegistry (e.g. SimpleMeterRegistry) is actually registered. A meaningful test pair is: (1) a minimal @SpringBootTest WITHOUT the annotation asserting no usable MeterRegistry bean / metrics export is suppressed, and (2) one WITH @AutoConfigureMetrics asserting a MeterRegistry bean is present and records a meter. The underlying toggle is the plain Spring Boot property spring.test.metrics.export (default false, from spring-configuration-metadata.json) — this is ordinary @SpringBootTest(properties=...) test code, not host environment/system-property setup, so it does not need a deterministic_setup entry.\",\n  \"risks\": [\"This is the first 'real' artifact in the spring-boot-*-test family to be onboarded here — its sibling POM-only starters (e.g. spring-boot-starter-micrometer-metrics-test) are already marked not-for-native-image with this artifact as the replacement, but there's no prior PR in this repo for a sibling like spring-boot-webmvc-test/spring-boot-restclient-test to cross-check the exact test shape against.\"]\n}\n```","ttft_ms":5697,"type":"result","duration_ms":207367,"uuid":"5303632c-97f4-4588-90f4-59b0bee6a8b0","ttft_stream_ms":2708,"time_to_request_ms":833,"first_content_frame_ms":2709,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}

